      "content": "Short coats for the upper body made in various forms and lengths, but usually no lower than the waist or upper hip; worn indoors or for light warmth and protection from the weather. [Source: Getty AAT] | a short and close-fitting upper garment of men and women; a jacket; especially coat of fence, a kind of sleeveless tunic or jacket, formerly worn by foot-soldiers and others, usually of leather quilted, and in later times often plated with iron (OED s.v. jack n.2 1a-1b)"
